.TH TUNPROXY 8 "August 2026" "TunProxy 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tunproxy \- manage a transparent TUN proxy through a pinned sing-box core
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tunproxy
.RI { on | off | status | setting }
.RI [ socks5://host:port ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tunproxy
creates a system TUN interface and forwards TCP traffic to a configured SOCKS5
upstream. It does not use shell proxy environment variables and does not manage
proxy nodes or subscriptions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B on
Verify or repair the managed core, validate the upstream, and enable the TUN.
Requires root privileges. Progress and stage messages are printed while the
core is downloaded, verified, started, and attached to the TUN interface.
.TP
.B off
Stop the managed core and remove its runtime state. Requires root privileges.
Stage messages identify the process termination and TUN interface cleanup.
.TP
.B status
Show the current state, upstream, managed core version, PID, and routing mode.
.TP
.B setting
Show or update the SOCKS5 upstream. Requires root privileges.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tunproxy/config
User configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/tunproxy/cores/1.13.18/sing-box
Verified private sing-box executable.
.TP
.I /run/tunproxy/
Runtime configuration, state, lock, and log files.
.TP
.I /var/cache/tunproxy/
Temporary sing-box archives. The download progress bar is printed to standard
error while an archive is being fetched.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Version 0.1 proxies TCP traffic. DNS is sent through DNS-over-HTTPS via the
SOCKS5 upstream. Other UDP traffic is rejected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip (8),
.BR curl (1)
